    {
      "id": "9ae43b44-6f61-4cbc-9dc4-06b48ae21491",
      "name": "Composable websites: MCP meets the block grid",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Composable websites: MCP meets the block grid",
      "docTypeId": "56026ff4-268b-4bd4-ab62-848bfeb3f751",
      "templateId": "ce572622-b2a1-40f6-8e47-4dd1ac318ec1",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Composable websites: MCP meets the block grid"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "Pages are no longer written — they are assembled. Structured blocks, negotiated over MCP, let an assistant compose layouts that editors still own."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "heroImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "c3a5e4b6-8d9f-4c7a-be23-99cc33dd4a03",
              "mediaKey": "9ae2ea74-9421-45fe-b056-3158540576b7",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "1099cf6a-1d94-46aa-91a0-f1d883f6cc7e",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "3ca23f7f-a90e-45bb-b024-064babda1185",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "36daf2e1-bedb-4a65-84c1-73a30ae40d19",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "11fa7216-5263-4955-80d9-45c664295fdf",
                "key": "1099cf6a-1d94-46aa-91a0-f1d883f6cc7e",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>A CMS page is not a document — it is a list of composable pieces: a hero, some prose, an image with a caption, a quote. Umbraco's block grid is exactly that contract, and MCP makes it machine-negotiable.</p><p>An assistant can inspect the schema, learn which blocks exist and which properties they carry, then assemble a page the same way an editor would click it together — without ever learning the CSS or the markup underneath.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "33e87ee9-2f8d-4963-bb8e-73324ab99973",
                "key": "3ca23f7f-a90e-45bb-b024-064babda1185",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "d4b6f5c7-9e0a-4d8b-cf34-aadd44ee5b04",
                        "mediaKey": "ef322854-4b4b-4d1c-b9ea-a4aee0758b74",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Blocks are like cubes: independent pieces that only become a structure through a shared contract. Photo: Shubham Dhage, Unsplash."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "11fa7216-5263-4955-80d9-45c664295fdf",
                "key": "36daf2e1-bedb-4a65-84c1-73a30ae40d19",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>The crucial part: the machine only fills in the content. The schema, the rendering views and the editorial guardrails stay human-owned. That is the promise of MCP in a CMS — automation where it helps, structure where it matters.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
